{"id": "EUVD-2026-82303", "enisaUuid": "2d49aad8-5d66-35b4-9ed8-f1a08beafd3a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/bridge: synopsys: dw-dp: Support unregistering the AUX channel\n\nThe DisplayPort AUX channel gets initialized and registered during\ndw_dp_bind(), but it is never unregistered, which may lead to resource\nleaks and/or use-after-free.\n\nAdd the missing dw_dp_unbind() function to allow the users of the\nlibrary to handle the required cleanup, i.e. unregister the AUX adapter.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:12:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:07:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b2bec2d4a769d5b7b8202123404c7cd1aec17861", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/48aaa495e24ce5aec3dc56706473b0bd4305a306", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ed04e8e2307f35b3d8d49a554faf5e72d3d224e6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93195", "GHSA-ffp4-w5gv-fphv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ccef435-02b9-3a46-b7c6-b205ec159c44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "4aea2c42-1b0a-354b-a696-8b7f911581e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5025462a-e7a0-3e1f-8bcd-467ec523b9ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "560f4b96-7ecb-3355-b8b7-d9bd155e2c6c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6aaebfa4-8229-3eaa-b531-16214daecd4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "86eecc3a9c2e06462f6a273fcd24150b6da787de <ed04e8e2307f35b3d8d49a554faf5e72d3d224e6"}, {"id": "f989a588-2335-3a0e-beb8-a18c5c51c0d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "86eecc3a9c2e06462f6a273fcd24150b6da787de <48aaa495e24ce5aec3dc56706473b0bd4305a306"}, {"id": "faab39d2-7f14-